QUESTION 6 : Why do software development teams create branches instead
of working directly on the main branch?
====================================================================

Interview Ready Answer

Software development teams create branches to isolate feature
development from the main branch. Each developer works on a
separate branch, allowing multiple features to be developed
independently without affecting the stable codebase. After the
feature is completed, tested, and reviewed, it is merged into
the main branch.

Definition

Branch:
An independent line of development used to implement features,
bug fixes, or experiments without affecting the main branch.

Purpose

• Isolate feature development
• Protect the main branch
• Enable parallel development
• Reduce merge conflicts
• Allow code review before merging

Important Keywords

• Feature Branch
• Stable Main Branch
• Parallel Development
• Pull Request
• Merge

Memory Trick

