QUESTION 8 : What is a Merge Conflict, and when does it occur?
====================================================================

Interview Ready Answer

A merge conflict occurs when Git cannot automatically merge
changes because two branches have modified the same part of the
same file. The developer must manually resolve the conflict
before completing the merge.

Definition

Merge Conflict:
A situation where Git cannot decide which version of the code
should be kept during a merge.

Purpose

• Prevent incorrect automatic merges
• Ensure developers manually verify conflicting changes
• Maintain code correctness

When Does It Occur?

• Same file modified
• Same lines modified
• Git cannot determine the correct version

How Is It Resolved?

• Resolve the conflicting code manually
• git add .
• git commit

Important Keywords

• Same File
• Same Lines
• Manual Resolution
• Git Cannot Auto Merge

Memory Trick

Same File + Same Lines = Merge Conflict

====================================================================
INTERVIEW TRAP
====================================================================

Q:
Will Git always create a merge conflict if two developers modify
the same file?

Answer:
No.

If they modify different parts of the file, Git can usually merge
the changes automatically. A conflict typically occurs when the
same part of the file is modified.

====================================================================
QUICK REVISION
====================================================================

• Merge Conflict = Git cannot auto merge.
• Usually occurs when the same lines are modified.
• Developer resolves it manually.
• After resolving → git add → git commit.

